    {
      "topLeftX": 50,
      "topLeftY": 167,
      "bottomRightX": 651,
      "bottomRightY": 201,
      "content": "The AcquisitionMode controls the mode of acquisition for the device. This mainly affects the number of frames captured in the Acquisition (SingleFrame, MultiFrame or Continuous).",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 50,
      "topLeftY": 207,
      "bottomRightX": 632,
      "bottomRightY": 240,
      "content": "The optional AcquisitionArm command is used to verify and freeze all parameters relevant for the image data capture. It prepares the device for the AcquisitionStart.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 50,
      "topLeftY": 248,
      "bottomRightX": 428,
      "bottomRightY": 265,
      "content": "The AcquisitionStart command is used to start the Acquisition.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 50,
      "topLeftY": 271,
      "bottomRightX": 628,
      "bottomRightY": 321,
      "content": "The AcquisitionStop command will stop the Acquisition at the end of the current Frame. It can be used in any acquisition mode and if the camera is waiting for a trigger, the pending Frame will be cancelled.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 50,
      "topLeftY": 328,
      "bottomRightX": 632,
      "bottomRightY": 363,
      "content": "The AcquisitionAbort command can be used to abort an Acquisition at any time. This will end the capture immediately without completing the current Frame.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 50,
      "topLeftY": 369,
      "bottomRightX": 541,
      "bottomRightY": 403,
      "content": "AcquisitionFrameCount controls the number of frames that will be captured when AcquisitionMode is MultiFrame.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 50,
      "topLeftY": 410,
      "bottomRightX": 543,
      "bottomRightY": 443,
      "content": "AcquisitionBurstFrameCount determines the length of each burst to capture if the FrameBurstStart trigger is enabled and the FrameBurstEnd trigger is disabled.",
